node_modules/
web-ext-artifacts/
dist/
*.log

# Captured Royal Road HTML: several megabytes, and re-derivable at any time.
# test/fixtures/README.md documents how to capture each one. The selector and
# DOM suites skip themselves with a named reason when these are absent.
#
# Ignored by directory rather than by extension, so a capture saved under a new
# name or a new subdirectory is still covered. A raw capture straight from the
# site carries a live __RequestVerificationToken; the committed README explains
# how to strip them, but nothing in here is meant to be committed at all.
test/fixtures/**
!test/fixtures/README.md

# Paste-ready store submission text, one file per release. Generated from the
# code, CHANGELOG and PRIVACY at release time; not shared, because it is a
# transcript of two dashboards' form fields rather than anything about the
# extension. .claude/skills/release/ says what each file has to contain.
store-submissions/

# Local editor and agent state
.claude/settings.local.json
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Firefox profile `npm start` reuses so you are not logging into Royal Road on
# every launch. It holds a real session, and web-ext rewrites its prefs on each
# run to allow remote debugging and unsigned add-ons, which makes it unsuitable
# for anything but this. `npm start -- --fresh` skips it entirely.
.dev-profile/

# Working notes for Claude Code. Deliberately not shared: they are reminders about
# how to work on this repo, not documentation. Anything a contributor needs goes in
# CONTRIBUTING.md instead. `.claude/skills/` holds the same notes, split out so the
# end-of-workflow ones (the release procedure, the store submission) are loaded only
# when they are needed rather than on every turn. Ignored as a directory so a note
# added under a new skill name is covered too.
#
# Only `.claude/skills/` — `.claude/settings.json` and `.claude/commands/` stay
# committable, because those would be project config a contributor could use.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/skills/
